<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Failaka Island</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Failaka</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Failaka is an island in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-gulf">Persian Gulf</a> off Kuwait City. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze-age">Bronze Age</a> it was an outpost of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dilmun">Dilmun</a> culture, with settlements, temples and seals of Dilmun type, and in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hellenistic-period">Hellenistic period</a> it held a fortress and temples under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucids</a>, when it was known as Ikaros. It has been largely uninhabited since the Iraqi invasion of 1990.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/failaka-island.jpg" alt="Failaka Island" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ரோஜா · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Beach_at_Failaka_Island.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
